{"id":"mahabharata-5-032","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":32,"title":"द्वात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 32 · Sanjaya reports to Dhritarashtra","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya returns to Hastinapura and, admitted at night, reproaches Dhritarashtra for following his son and for the ruin he has brought on his house. Exhausted from the journey, he says he will deliver Yudhishthira's message in the assembly at dawn, and goes to rest.","kn":"ಹಸ್ತಿನಾಪುರಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳಿದ ಸಂಜಯನು ರಾತ್ರಿ ಪ್ರವೇಶ ಪಡೆದು, ಮಗನನ್ನು ಅನುಸರಿಸಿ ಕುಲಕ್ಕೆ ವಿನಾಶ ತಂದದ್ದಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನನ್ನು ಆಕ್ಷೇಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪ್ರಯಾಣದಿಂದ ದಣಿದ ಅವನು ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ ಸಭೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ಸಂದೇಶ ತಿಳಿಸುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ವಿಶ್ರಮಿಸಲು ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सञ्जय हस्तिनापुर लौटकर रात में प्रवेश पाते हैं और पुत्र का अनुसरण कर कुल पर विनाश लाने के लिए धृतराष्ट्र को उलाहना देते हैं। यात्रा से थके वे कहते हैं कि भोर में सभा में युधिष्ठिर का सन्देश सुनाएँगे, और विश्राम करने चले जाते हैं।","te":"హస్తినాపురానికి తిరిగివచ్చిన సంజయుడు రాత్రి ప్రవేశం పొంది, కుమారుని అనుసరించి కులానికి వినాశం తెచ్చినందుకు ధృతరాష్ట్రుని నిందిస్తాడు. ప్రయాణంతో అలసిన అతడు ఉదయం సభలో యుధిష్ఠిరుని సందేశం వినిపిస్తానని చెప్పి విశ్రమించడానికి వెళ్తాడు.","ta":"ஹஸ்தினாபுரம் திரும்பிய ஸஞ்ஜயன் இரவில் உள்ளே அனுமதிக்கப்பட்டு, மகனைப் பின்பற்றிக் குலத்துக்கு அழிவு தேடியதற்காக த்ருதராஷ்டிரனைக் கடிகிறான். பயணத்தால் களைத்த அவன் விடியலில் சபையில் யுதிஷ்டிரரின் செய்தியைச் சொல்வதாகக் கூறி ஓய்வெடுக்கச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"സഞ്ജയൻ ഹസ്തിനപുരത്തെത്തി, രാത്രിയിൽ അകത്തുകടന്ന് മകനെ പിന്തുടർന്നതിനും അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ കുലത്തിന് വരുത്തിയ നാശത്തിനും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരെ ശാസിക്കുന്നു. യാത്രാക്ഷീണത്താൽ, പുലർച്ചെ സദസ്സിൽ യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ സന്ദേശം അറിയിക്കാമെന്ന് പറഞ്ഞ് അദ്ദേഹം വിശ്രമിക്കാൻ പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.32; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"संजययानपर्व","titleEn":"Sanjayayana Parva (Sanjaya's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अनुज्ञातः पाण्डवेन प्रययौ संजयस्तदा ।\nशासनं धृतराष्ट्रस्य सर्वं कृत्वा महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having carried out all the instructions of great-souled Dhritarashtra, Sanjaya then set out with the Pandava's leave."}},{"n":2,"text":"संप्राप्य हास्तिनपुरं शीघ्रं च प्रविवेश ह ।\nअन्तःपुरमुपस्थाय द्वाःस्थं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He reached Hastinapura and entered it quickly; coming to the inner palace, he spoke to the doorkeeper."}},{"n":3,"text":"आचक्ष्व मां धृतराष्ट्राय द्वाःस्थ\nउपागतं पाण्डवानां सकाशात् ।\nजागर्ति चेदभिवदेस्त्वं हि क्षत्तः\nप्रविशेयं विदितो भूमिपस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Doorkeeper, announce me to Dhritarashtra: I have come from the Pandavas. If he is awake, tell him, and I will go in with the king's knowledge, Kshatta.\""}},{"text":"द्वाःस्थ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The doorkeeper said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"संजयोऽयं भूमिपते नमस्ते\nदिदृक्षया द्वारमुपागतस्ते ।\nप्राप्तो दूतः पाण्डवानां सकाशा-\nत्प्रशाधि राजन्किमयं करोतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, this is Sanjaya; he bows to you. He has come to your door wishing to see you, an envoy arrived from the Pandavas. Command, king, what is he to do?"}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"आचक्ष्व मां सुखिनं काल्यमस्मै\nप्रवेश्यतां स्वागतं संजयाय ।\nन चाहमेतस्य भवाम्यकाल्यः\nस मे कस्माद्द्वारि तिष्ठेत क्षत्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell Sanjaya I am well and that he may be admitted tomorrow; welcome to him. I am never unavailable to him, so why should he wait at my door, Kshatta?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"ततः प्रविश्यानुमते नृपस्य\nमहद्वेश्म प्राज्ञशूरार्यगुप्तम् ।\nसिंहासनस्थं पार्थिवमाससाद\nवैचित्रवीर्यं प्राञ्जलिः सूतपुत्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, entering with the king's leave the great palace guarded by the wise, the brave and the noble, the charioteer's son, with folded hands, came to the king, Vichitravirya's son, seated on his throne."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"संजयोऽहं भूमिपते नमस्ते\nप्राप्तोऽस्मि गत्वा नरदेव पाण्डवान् ।\nअभिवाद्य त्वां पाण्डुपुत्रो मनस्वी\nयुधिष्ठिरः कुशलं चान्वपृच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Sanjaya, king; I bow to you. I have gone to the Pandavas, lord of men, and returned. The high-minded Yudhishthira, son of Pandu, saluted you and asked after your welfare."}},{"n":8,"text":"स ते पुत्रान्पृच्छति प्रीयमाणः\nकच्चित्पुत्रैः प्रीयसे नप्तृभिश्च ।\nतथा सुहृद्भिः सचिवैश्च राज-\nन्ये चापि त्वामुपजीवन्ति तैश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delighted, he asks after your sons: I hope you are happy with your sons and grandsons, with your friends and counselors, and with all who live on you, king."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"अभ्येत्य त्वां तात वदामि संजय\nअजातशत्रुं च सुखेन पार्थम् ।\nकच्चित्स राजा कुशली सपुत्रः\nसहामात्यः सानुजः कौरवाणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear Sanjaya, I come back to you and ask about the peaceful Ajatashatru, the son of Pritha: is that king well, with his sons, counselors and younger brothers, among the Kauravas?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"सहामात्यः कुशली पाण्डुपुत्रो\nभूयश्चातो यच्च तेऽग्रे मनोऽभूत् ।\nनिर्णिक्तधर्मार्थकरो मनस्वी\nबहुश्रुतो दृष्टिमाञ्शीलवांश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Pandu is well with his counselors, and even more than you hoped. He is high-minded, learned, far-seeing and virtuous, and he has purified his dharma and his dealings in wealth."}},{"n":11,"text":"परं धर्मात्पाण्डवस्यानृशंस्यं\nधर्मः परो वित्तचयान्मतोऽस्य ।\nसुखप्रिये धर्महीने न पार्थो-\nऽनुरुध्यते भारत तस्य विद्धि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Pandu holds gentleness higher than dharma itself, and dharma higher than piling up wealth. Know, Bharata, that Partha does not follow what is merely pleasant or what lacks dharma."}},{"n":12,"text":"परप्रयुक्तः पुरुषो विचेष्टते\nसूत्रप्रोता दारुमयीव योषा ।\nइमं दृष्ट्वा नियमं पाण्डवस्य\nमन्ये परं कर्म दैवं मनुष्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man driven by another moves as a wooden puppet strung on threads. Seeing this restraint of the Pandava, I think fate is stronger than human effort."}},{"n":13,"text":"इमं च दृष्ट्वा तव कर्मदोषं\nपादोदर्कं घोरमवर्णरूपम् ।\nयावन्नरः कामयतेऽतिकाल्यं\nतावन्नरोऽयं लभते प्रशंसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And seeing the fault of your own conduct, dreadful, with a bitter end, and ugly in form: a man earns praise only as long as he longs for what is beyond his time."}},{"n":14,"text":"अजातशत्रुस्तु विहाय पापं\nजीर्णां त्वचं सर्प इवासमर्थाम् ।\nविरोचतेऽहार्यवृत्तेन धीरो\nयुधिष्ठिरस्त्वयि पापं विसृज्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Ajatashatru, having cast off sin as a snake sheds its worn-out skin, shines with unstolen conduct; Yudhishthira, steady, has laid the sin on you."}},{"n":15,"text":"अङ्गात्मनः कर्म निबोध राज-\nन्धर्मार्थयुक्तादार्यवृत्तादपेतम् ।\nउपक्रोशं चेह गतोऽसि राज-\nन्नोहेश्च पापं प्रसजेदमुत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know, my friend, the deed of this person, which departs from noble conduct joined to dharma and wealth. You have fallen into reproach here, king, and you will bind sin for the hereafter if you persist in it."}},{"n":16,"text":"स त्वमर्थं संशयितं विना तै-\nराशंससे पुत्रवशानुगोऽद्य ।\nअधर्मशब्दश्च महान्पृथिव्यां\nनेदं कर्म त्वत्समं भारताग्र्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"You expect gain, while they are in doubt, following the will of your sons now. A great word of adharma is on the earth: this deed is not worthy of you, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":17,"text":"हीनप्रज्ञो दौष्कुलेयो नृशंसो\nदीर्घवैरी क्षत्रविद्यास्वधीरः ।\nएवंधर्मा नापदः संतितीर्षे-\nद्धीनवीर्यो यश्च भवेदशिष्टः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man of small wisdom, of bad birth, cruel, long in enmity, unsteady in the sciences of the warrior, one so inclined, weak and ill-conducted, does not hope to cross over a calamity."}},{"n":18,"text":"कुले जातो धर्मवान्यो यशस्वी\nबहुश्रुतः सुखजीवी यतात्मा ।\nधर्मार्थयोर्ग्रथितयोर्बिभर्ति\nनान्यत्र दिष्टस्य वशादुपैति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But he who is born in a family, righteous, famed, learned, who lives happily and is self-controlled, who holds dharma and wealth together, does not come under any other thing except by the power of fate."}},{"n":19,"text":"कथं हि मन्त्राग्र्यधरो मनीषी\nधर्मार्थयोरापदि संप्रणेता ।\nएवंयुक्तः सर्वमन्त्रैरहीनो\nअनानृशंस्यं कर्म कुर्यादमूढः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could a wise man who bears the chief counsel, who guides dharma and wealth in distress, being so equipped and lacking no counsel, undeluded, do a cruel deed?"}},{"n":20,"text":"तवापीमे मन्त्रविदः समेत्य\nसमासते कर्मसु नित्ययुक्ताः ।\nतेषामयं बलवान्निश्चयश्च\nकुरुक्षयार्थे निरयो व्यपादि ॥","meaning":{"en":"These counselors of yours too, knowing the counsels, sit together, always engaged in their tasks. Their strong resolve has become a hell for the destruction of the Kurus."}},{"n":21,"text":"अकालिकं कुरवो नाभविष्य-\nन्पापेन चेत्पापमजातशत्रुः ।\nइच्छेज्जातु त्वयि पापं विसृज्य\nनिन्दा चेयं तव लोकेऽभविष्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus would not have perished before their time if Ajatashatru, wishing to repay sin with sin, had ever wished to throw his sin upon you; and then this censure would have been yours in the world."}},{"n":22,"text":"किमन्यत्र विषयादीश्वराणां\nयत्र पार्थः परलोकं ददर्श ।\nअत्यक्रामत्स तथा संमतः स्या-\nन्न संशयो नास्ति मनुष्यकारः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What, besides their realm, belongs to the rulers? Partha has seen the other world; he has gone beyond, and he would be honored thus. There is no doubt that human effort exists."}},{"n":23,"text":"एतान्गुणान्कर्मकृतानवेक्ष्य\nभावाभावौ वर्तमानावनित्यौ ।\nबलिर्हि राजा पारमविन्दमानो\nनान्यत्कालात्कारणं तत्र मेने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing these virtues made by deeds, with existence and non-existence both passing and impermanent, King Bali, finding no far shore, thought nothing else but time the cause there."}},{"n":24,"text":"चक्षुः श्रोत्रे नासिका त्वक्च जिह्वा\nज्ञानस्यैतान्यायतनानि जन्तोः ।\nतानि प्रीतान्येव तृष्णाक्षयान्ते\nतान्यव्यथो दुःखहीनः प्रणुद्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eye, ear, nose, skin and tongue are the seats of knowledge in a creature. They are satisfied only at the end of craving; free of pain, one without grief should drive them away."}},{"n":25,"text":"न त्वेव मन्ये पुरुषस्य कर्म\nसंवर्तते सुप्रयुक्तं यथावत् ।\nमातुः पितुः कर्मणाभिप्रसूतः\nसंवर्धते विधिवद्भोजनेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet I do not think that a man's deed, well done, turns out exactly as intended: one born by the deed of mother and father grows up by proper nourishment."}},{"n":26,"text":"प्रियाप्रिये सुखदुःखे च राज-\nन्निन्दाप्रशंसे च भजेत एनम् ।\nपरस्त्वेनं गर्हयतेऽपराधे\nप्रशंसते साधुवृत्तं तमेव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear and not dear, happiness and sorrow, blame and praise, king, all attend him. Another reproaches him for a fault, and praises the very same good conduct."}},{"n":27,"text":"स त्वा गर्हे भारतानां विरोधा-\nदन्तो नूनं भवितायं प्रजानाम् ।\nनो चेदिदं तव कर्मापराधा-\nत्कुरून्दहेत्कृष्णवर्त्मेव कक्षम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I blame you, because of the quarrel among the Bharatas, an end of the people will surely come, unless this deed of yours, from your fault, burns the Kurus like a fire taking a dry thicket."}},{"n":28,"text":"त्वमेवैको जातपुत्रेषु राज-\nन्वशं गन्ता सर्वलोके नरेन्द्र ।\nकामात्मनां श्लाघसे द्यूतकाले\nनान्यच्छमात्पश्य विपाकमस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you alone among fathers of sons will go under the sway of the world; you praise those ruled by desire at the time of the dice. See no result of this other than peace."}},{"n":29,"text":"अनाप्तानां प्रग्रहात्त्वं नरेन्द्र\nतथाप्तानां निग्रहाच्चैव राजन् ।\nभूमिं स्फीतां दुर्बलत्वादनन्तां\nन शक्तस्त्वं रक्षितुं कौरवेय ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, by seizing those who were not yours and by confining those who were, you, descendant of Kuru, are unable to protect the vast earth, grown wide, because of your weakness."}},{"n":30,"text":"अनुज्ञातो रथवेगावधूतः\nश्रान्तो निपद्ये शयनं नृसिंह ।\nप्रातः श्रोतारः कुरवः सभाया-\nमजातशत्रोर्वचनं समेताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dismissed, shaken by the speed of the chariot, I am tired, tiger among men, and will lie on my bed. Tomorrow morning the Kurus, gathered in the assembly, will hear the words of Ajatashatru."}}]}]}